(
  /* A bb_term renders as a BADGE, and the labels screen is a badge surface. The human:
     "with the labels I see badges rather than the rows." So no row component exists for a term at
     all.

     ONE VOCABULARY, NOT TWO. This mapping and the labels screen used to carry `bb_capability_tags`
     beside `bb_labels`; that bundle is RETIRED BY DECISION at BB-338's second coding gate, its
     mapping deleted and its entry in `data-model.yml` replaced by a note recording the retirement.
     Removing the actual Drupal bundle is `config/sync` + recipe work and is deliberately not part of
     this ticket (C11), so the config object and the fixture file are both left standing.

     THERE IS NO VARIANT ANY MORE, AND THAT ANSWERED THE QUESTION THIS PARAGRAPH USED TO ARGUE.
     `badge` carried four variants — `state`, `token`, `label`, `priority` — and this mapping picked
     `label` over the other two because `state` was unpilled plain text, which made a whole screen of
     labels read as a column of words, and `token` was the quiet counter chip that annotates another
     value, which under-weighted the subject of the screen. All four collapsed into `tone`: the badge
     has ONE shape now, a tinted pill, so both failure modes are gone by construction rather than by
     picking correctly. `tone: neutral` is a label's tone — a term names itself and carries no state.

     `list_item` IS SET HERE BECAUSE THE SCREEN'S CONTAINER IS A LIST. The labels surface puts these
     badges directly inside `zone` with `list: true`, which puts `role="list"` on their parent, and
     `role="list"`/`role="listitem"` must be direct parent and child or a browser drops both roles.
     The badge cannot know where it was placed, so the placer says so.

     MOVED FROM `full`, NOT REWRITTEN THERE. `full` is an entity's OWN SCREEN and `teaser` is its row
     in a list; a term has no screen of its own, so it has no full rendering, and this file was only
     ever filed under the wrong view mode. `git mv` rather than a delete-plus-add, so the move is what
     the diff shows.

     ONE CORRECTION CAME WITH THE MOVE, and it is worth naming because the spec's own Fact 11 has it
     backwards. That fact claims this mapping emitted `badge` while the `designbook/sync/` generator
     for the same name emitted `label`, and reads the pair as pre-existing drift. Neither half is
     true: both emitted `bb_theme:form_label` — the FORM LABEL component, "Form label rendered inside a
     form element's label slot", whose default variant is an uppercase eyebrow above a text input.
     There was no drift; there was one wrong component in two places. A taxonomy term is not a form
     label, and C14 requires the vocabulary to render through `badge`, so the component name is
     corrected here. `label`'s two props went with it: `badge` has no slots and takes its text as the
     `label` PROP.

     A BADGE READS `name` ONLY. A term's `description` and `weight` are therefore not rendered
     anywhere by this ticket, and no term edit surface exists — the screen's `[+]` and its badges are
     inert, like every other action here. The section brief is corrected in the same change rather
     than left promising three fields. Whoever gives these pickers an endpoint owns the term edit
     surface along with it.

     The `designbook/sync/` generator bound to `core.entity_view_display.bb_term.bb_labels.full`
     is left exactly as it is, and that is a decision rather than an oversight: repairing it is a
     Drupal config change, which this ticket does not make. It is now a generator for a view mode
     this mapping no longer claims. */
  [
    {
      "component": "$DESIGNBOOK_COMPONENT_NAMESPACE:badge",
      "props": {
        "label": name,
        "tone": "neutral",
        "list_item": true
      }
    }
  ]
)
